      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-225077",
      ":question/problem": "Let $f$ be the Boolean function of two variables defined as\n$f(x_{1}, x_{2}) = max{x_{1} \\cdot x_{2}, x_{1}}$.\nComplete the following table corresponding to $f$.\n\n| $x_{1}$ | $x_{2}$ | $f$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| $0$ | $0$ | {{field-1}} |\n| $0$ | $1$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $1$ | $0$ | {{field-3}} |\n| $1$ | $1$ | {{field-4}} |"
